# UI, theme, i18n

## UI

- Mobile-first, few elements, generous whitespace, large touch targets
- Fast access to add-food
- Desktop is supported, not prioritized
- Seasonal theme must not change UI structure — colors and light accents only

## Styles

- No `<style>` blocks in Vue SFCs
- Views → `src/styles/views/{route-name}.css` (same name as `ROUTE_NAMES`)
- Components → `src/styles/components/{kebab-component-name}.css`
- Import CSS from `<script setup>`
- Colors only via theme CSS variables

## Seasonal theme

Date → season (constants, not hardcoded in components) → CSS variables from `src/styles/themes/`.
The user does not pick a theme. Keep logic isolated (`composables` + `stores/theme.ts`).

- autumn: yellow / gold / orange / red
- winter: blue / light blue / white
- spring: green / aquamarine / pink
- summer: berry / yellow / dark green

## i18n

- Languages: `uk`, `en`. Switch without a full reload
- Copy lives in `src/locales/{uk,en}/*.json`, not in templates
- Every new button / error / label goes into both locales at once

```vue
<!-- BAD --><button>Save</button>
<!-- GOOD --><button>{{ t('common.save') }}</button>
```

## Async actions

Required: loading, disabled, success, error. The user always knows what is happening.

Especially: login, register, add food, AI, upload, save meal, recommendations, profile update.

## AI in the UI

Show that the result is an **estimate**, not a medically exact value. Allow editing calories before save. No harsh advice when daily calories are low.
